\begin{didyouknow}{Finding a Lost Planet}
On 1 January 1801 Giuseppe Piazzi discovered Ceres. He tracked it for only about six weeks before it was lost in the Sun's glare. The 24-year-old Carl Friedrich Gauss used those few observations to predict where it would reappear, and astronomers found it close to his prediction around New Year 1802. Adrien-Marie Legendre was the first to publish least squares, in 1805.
\end{didyouknow}
