\begin{didyouknow}{Taming Ill-Posed Problems}
Andrey Tikhonov studied unstable inverse problems from the 1940s, and in 1963 he proposed adding a penalty term to stabilize them, now called Tikhonov regularization. Statisticians Arthur Hoerl and Robert Kennard independently popularized the same idea in 1970 as ridge regression. Both trade a little bias for a large reduction in noise amplification, the trade you will meet when fitting potentials to spectra.
\end{didyouknow}
